{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790549166,"nonce":"MTfknzXaiAkJ6OsDB8H1VLoCOHs=","message":"Lowered: a Haxe try on wasm is now an exception handler (per-trap catchswitch catching __c_longjmp, calls in the region as invokes), and trap functions are no longer optnone on wasm. TryBench on the Mac under ash run: try-in-loop 71 -\u003e 27 ns, try-per-call 55 -\u003e 37 ns, plain loop 1-1.5 ns. What remains is hlp_setup_trap_jit + hlp_remove_trap_jit (replacing them with a local buffer took the old arm from 55 to 29 ns per call), and the per-call shadow frame. Traps found on the way: the runtime throws with a copy of the buffer (so the catch compares a token in its first word); one catch block per function trips an LLVM backend bug when a handler's calls unwind into it; -wasm-enable-eh is required or the backend drops invokes; a rethrow leaves an exnref live that the fiber transform refuses to resume across (threads trapped), so unmatched jumps are thrown anew; ash_wasm_link wrote every ref type as funcref. Conformance: unit 1069/1069 under wasm and wasm-fibers, threads 22/22 under wasm-fibers.","files":null}]}